INT. NORTHSTAR WEATHER STATION - COMMON ROOM - NIGHT

Steel walls, wool blankets, a single heater ticking. Frost on the window. Instruments blink on a long table. Wind howls round the corners of the building.

GUNNAR BERG, 50s, beard, captain's cap, sits at the radio. PALOMA REYES, 30s, climatologist, parka zipped to the chin, turns pages in a logbook. REGGIE OYELOWO, 25, mechanic, sits on the floor and wraps his hands in a tea towel.

GUNNAR
(to the room)
Right. Rations. We have six days of food.

PALOMA
Gunnar, it's seven.

GUNNAR
Six, if Reggie eats.

REGGIE
Reggie is standing right here.

GUNNAR
Reggie is sitting right there.

PALOMA
Reggie, how are your hands?

REGGIE
Cold.

PALOMA
Frostbite?

REGGIE
Just cold. I think.

PALOMA
Let me see.

REGGIE
Leave it, Paloma.

PALOMA
Reggie.

He unwraps the towel and shows her. Pink, swollen, but sound. She nods.

PALOMA (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Okay. Okay. Not yet.

GUNNAR
(into the radio)
Base, Northstar. Do you read?

BASE (V.O.)
(radio, static)
...Northstar... storm... hold position...

GUNNAR
We're holding. How long?

BASE (V.O.)
(radio)
...seventy-two hours...

GUNNAR
Seventy-two. Understood.

He switches off the set. Silence. Even the wind seems to listen.

GUNNAR (CONT'D)
Three days.

REGGIE
Is that bad?

GUNNAR
It's three days.

PALOMA
Gunnar, you said six days of food.

GUNNAR
Then it's three days of waiting and three days of margin.

PALOMA
That's thin.

GUNNAR
It's what we have.

Reggie hugs his knees.

REGGIE
Does anybody want to play cards?

Paloma looks at Gunnar. Gunnar looks at Reggie. He takes off his cap.

GUNNAR
Deal.
